{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\np='verify_explore_test.go';s=open(p).read().replace('TestAssuranceVerifyNonvoterExplore','TestAssuranceVerifyNonvoterEligibility')\ns=s.replace('future:=leader.VerifyLeader()','future:=leader.VerifyLeader()\\\\n assuranceVerifyEvent(map[string]interface{}{\\\"event\\\":\\\"admitted\\\",\\\"operation\\\":\\\"verify-1\\\",\\\"policy\\\":\\\"only_nonvoter_append_replies\\\"})')\ns=s.replace('errText:=\\\"\\\";if err\"'!=nil {errText=err.Error()}'\"','errText:=\\\"\\\";if err\"'!=nil {errText=err.Error()}'\"\\\\n  eligible:=1;totalVoters:=0\\\\n  for _,server:=range membership.Servers {if server.Suffrage==Voter {totalVoters++;if server.ID\"'!=leader.localID && positive[server.ID]>0 {eligible++}}}'\"\\\\n  quorum:=totalVoters/2+1')\ns=s.replace('\\\"success\\\":err==nil,','\\\"success\\\":err==nil,\\\"completed\\\":true,\\\"eligible_voter_quorum\\\":eligible>=quorum,\\\"eligible_voter_support\\\":eligible,\\\"quorum\\\":quorum,')\nopen('verify_fixed_test.go','w').write(s)\nPY\ncat > build_check.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nr=json.load(open('../research.json'));q=r['candidates'][0]['question'];q['unknowns']=['Fresh fixed execution and correspondence must determine whether the constructed callback history satisfies the scoped voter-eligibility obligation.','A second leader and stale FSM read are independent unmeasured consequences.'];q['disposition']='ready_for_check'\nclaim='C-verify-eligible';binding='BD-verify-register'\nexpect=['M-api-verify','M-suffrage-contract','M-lease']\nimpl=['M-verify-register','M-verify-vote','M-notify','M-consume','M-leader','M-heartbeat']\nderivation='M-api-verify promises a leadership check usable to prevent stale reads. M-suffrage-contract distinguishes voters from nonvoters; M-lease and quorumSize use voter membership for authority support. The scoped necessary eligibility rule is that nonvoter callbacks cannot substitute for voter confirmations in the voter-threshold verification procedure. It does not require successful verification without quorum or claim a numeric completion deadline. This is a composed responsibility inferred from these interfaces and authority mechanisms, not an explicit statement that this execution contains a stale read.'\nground=dict(source_ids=impl,expectation_ids=expect,derivation=derivation,applicability='Fixed valid membership, eligible local voter elected by actual voter handlers, pending public VerifyLeader under that tenure. No configuration transition, corruption or Byzantine responses.',unresolved=[],alternatives=['Lease may independently reject later; it cannot change the eligibility of support counted toward this verification.','Actual application data may still be fresh in this prefix.'])\nob=dict(id=claim,kind='obligation',concern='implementation_semantics',description='In a fixed valid configuration, a leader verification that completes successfully by reaching its voter-derived quorum threshold must have support from a majority of configured voters (including the local voter); positive confirmations from configured nonvoters must not substitute for missing voter support.',source_ids=impl+expect,scope=dict(description='Membership eligibility of the quorum-confirmation procedure backing VerifyLeader, within one elected leader tenure and fixed membership.',assumptions=['Correct real RPC handlers and reliable in-memory storage','Network may fail requests to selected voters while nonvoter is reachable','Finite scheduling may delay follower election timers; leader lease remains enabled'],excluded=['End-to-end linearizability or second leader','Unbounded liveness','Membership changes','Crashes or malicious messages']),pending=[],grounding=ground)\nbd=dict(id=binding,material_id='M-verify-register',symbol='verifyLeader',start_line=965,end_line=987,description='Initializes voter-derived threshold and registers pending future on replication workers.',pending=[],associations=[dict(claim_id=claim,source_ids=impl+expect,rationale=derivation)])\nfeedback=dict(ref_ids=['88e182240e5f44df859d5d7eb39d835e','e0d835087411436692c37634f67da4b2','M-verify-register','M-verify-vote'],answered='Exploration e0d835087411436692c37634f67da4b2 completed: prepared leader term 2, 3 voters/1 nonvoter, no replication before blocked-voter policy; result success=true with positive_append_responses={n:1}, no positive voter responses and state Leader term 2. Thus no hidden local guard excluded nonvoter support in this prefix. These observations remain exploration, not formal evidence.',remaining=['Fresh execution of fixed check and checker correspondence are required.','No second leader or stale FSM read was observed.'],understanding='updated',rationale='The actual public-future result motivates a scoped local eligibility check, not a whole-cluster safety conclusion.')\ncand=dict(action='obligation',candidate_id=r['candidates'][0]['id'],rationale='Fix voter eligibility of the verification accounting procedure as the local responsibility, preserving separate unmeasured global consequence.',question=q,obligation=ob,bindings=[bd])\nlegality=dict(source_ids=['M-bootstrap','M-start','M-skip-start','M-elect-producer','M-election','M-leader','M-trans-contract','M-heartbeat','M-append','M-api-verify','M-future'],expectation_ids=['M-api-verify'],derivation='Bootstrap each node with the same valid 3-voter/1-nonvoter configuration. NewRaft skipStartup is a testing scheduler boundary; follower pumps run actual processRPC serially. Actual runCandidate/electSelf request real persisted votes from voters. No replication starts before the transport policy blocks b/c appends. Only then runLeader starts and public VerifyLeader is enqueued. Thus no pre-policy successful voter append can race registration. The wrapper returns transport errors for voter appends and disables optional pipeline; nonvoter requests traverse rea